<title>PHILIPPINES: Indonesia gets $44 mln loan from ADB.</title>
<headline>Indonesia gets $44 mln loan from ADB.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Asian Development Bank (ADB) said on Friday it had approved a $44 million loan to Indonesia.</p>
<p>The loan will fund the introduction of environmentally friendly pest management practices to farmers. The total cost of the project is estimated at $79.6 million.</p>
<p>The ADB said the loan would be payable over 25 years with an annual interest rate of 6.82 percent.</p>
